<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3915" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέα</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰλ]</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέη</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλη, ἀλέομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>avoiding, escape</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγύθι μοι θάνατος . . οὐδ᾽ ἀλέη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.301
				</span></i>
			 (not in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἔστιν ἀ. οὐδὲ σκέπη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>: c.gen., <i>shelter from</i> athing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑετοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					545
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			and 
				Ion.
			 word. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέα</span></b>  (B),
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰλ]</span>, 
				Ion.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέη</span></b> , ἡ, 
				contr.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Androm.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.33
			</span></i>, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				18.11
			</span></i> :—<i>warmth, heat</i>, of fire, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.23
			</span></i> (not in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Mis.</u>
				341c
			</span></i>; generally, <i>warmth</i>, or <i>warm spot</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἀλέῃ γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VM</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				141
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσενεγκὼν ἐς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρέεσθαι περιπάτοις ἐν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Vict.</u>
					3.68
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἀ. κατακείμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					541
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέας καὶ ψύχους</span>
			<i>in heat</i> and cold, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Erx.</u>
				401d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1148a8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνῖγος καὶ ἀ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1026b34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς ἀ.</span> in the
				<i>hot season</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				939b9
			</span></i>: later, <i>animal, bodily heat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.131d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				3.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				48
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				24
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i>; generally, <i>source of warmth</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἔριον ἡμῖν κόσμος καὶ ἀ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				1.21
			</span></i>, etc.: in pl., <i>fomentations</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i> Trall.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Febr.</u>
				3
			</span></i>.</div>
